A||||12||JohnnyK||Saw the coolest thing today!||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||01-31-2001||02:41 PM||||Walked outside this morning, and I heard this sizzling/electric noise. I looked up, and there was this squirrel getting fried. I'm watching the thing for about 10 seconds, and finally it drops till it's hanging on by 1 paw, then it falls 30-40 feet head first onto this ice bank (it's winter, but been thawing and freezing). Anyways, I assume it's dead, but then it starts breathing in short gasps, and it's eyes are glazed over (kind looks like he got hit with 30,000 volts..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> He starts sliding down the ice bank, so I gie him a little tap so that he doesn't go falling off another ledge, and he rolls over, and starts limping away on 2 feet. Then after a car passes, he starts running and takes off..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||01-31-2001||02:52 PM||||I can't believe he is alive. When they get fried over here they blow the fuse at the pole and the electric company has to come out. They usually are on fire when they fall too. Poor things.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shiner||01-31-2001||03:07 PM||||Don't feel bad about it!  I WISH some of those country monkeys around here would bite on the powerlines more often.  It's like the fourth of July, but more smelly.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||01-31-2001||03:47 PM||||Nah, didn't feel too bad. Getting used to it. A few months ago my cat was eating a dove while it was still alive, so I had to shmuck it's head with the end of a broomstick (the dove, not the cat) and a few weeks ago we nailed a deer with the van no the way home from a  christmas thing, and I had to sit there while that thing died, so it's getting to be a regular occurance..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm impressed it's not dead. It hung there while being electrocuted for a good 10 seconds!||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||01-31-2001||04:39 PM||||that squirrel wasnt driving a Fiero was he....would explain a lot, lol||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||01-31-2001||05:37 PM||||I'm surprised that he lived. Usually, they are dead before they even hit the ground.  And they usually do blow the fuse, and put at least a couple of customers in the dark. (whoever is fed from that particular transformer). Makes a helluva bang.  <BR>Power Company guys affectionately refer to squirrels as "Pole Rats".  <BR>BTW... most of the distribution lines (just before the transformer) around here are around 14,400 volts. I don't think he took a direct shot. He'd have been toast. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||01-31-2001||06:28 PM||||Shiner--What have you got against monkeys???????  Be nice or else.||||reg||1
Z||000007||btoth||01-31-2001||11:53 PM||||Squirrel story:  My junior year at high school, a squirrel got electricuted on the power lines outside the building. Somehow it shorted out the circuit breaker (fuse box? I don't know for sure...) but I was in the gym locker room changing for class when we saw smoke comming from the back of the locker room.  (Which was were the breaker was.)  We thought it was a fire so the school was evactuated and the fire trucks came...  After the fire trucks left and we were allowed back inside we were told over the PA that it was all caused by a squirrel.. they found it's chared remains under the power lines.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  (So sad... squirrels are my favorite animal!)||||reg||10
Z||000008||Seanh||02-01-2001||12:24 AM||||A few years ago at my grandparents house in FL, My parents and I were staying there. They had a pestering cat that wouldnt leave them alone. They fed it because they felt so sorry for it. It was always getting in their house and one night the power went out. We assumed it was a power company problem and went to bed. Next moring, still no power. Called the power company and they said there was nothing wrong with that section of town. So they called some one out after unsuccessful attempts to reset the breakers. They found what was left of that cat in the roof. He got stuck in the wires comming into the house, high voltage suckers, and he got fried.||||reg||1
Z||000009||StuGood||02-02-2001||12:14 AM||||Reminds me - one time while in the garage, saw somebody walking through my back yard.  Wondered what was up, so went into the yard and there were a couple of power company guys standing under a pole (that had a transformer on it).<P>One of them told me they had just installed a "squirrel guard" (I think that's what they called it). Apparently, they mount a small bare wire near the top of the pole, and hook it to the power supply in such a way that the wire has a small amount of juice in it. Enough "zap" to discourage squirrels, but not so much that I get quick-fried squirrels lying around underneath the pole.  Keeps them from blowing fuses, transformers and such.  I thought it sounded like a pretty cool idea  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.   ||||reg||7
Z||000010||loafer87gt||02-02-2001||10:28 AM||||The biggest pests in my opinion are crows and magpies, I can't stand them! We used to have some neat Purple Martins in our yard, and the damn magpies harassed them so much they left. It was kinda funny last year, I was out of shotgun ammo, so I picked one of the suckers off with a hunting dart in the head from my .177 airrifle. Scared the crap out of the stupid bird (literally), but I still see the same crow  flying around the yard, with, yep, a red dart sticking out of his melon.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroLisa||02-02-2001||05:22 PM||||Alright back in my days in High school  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, so uh lets see my junior year 2 years ago, I was sitting in Physics when the lights in the whole school out. A black squirrel did the same thing, only it fried out a transformer or something along those lines. We got out of school early (like at 10 am), named the poor little squirrel Sparky.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
